jobs.description:
Are you looking for a fulltime job in logistics? Would you like to work in a modern, international warehouse where fashion and clothing products are shipped to customers all over the world? Then this opportunity could be perfect for you!

For a large logistics clothing warehouse in Lelystad, we are looking for motivated Production Workers, Warehouse Operatives, and Logistics Associates. You will become part of a friendly international team where teamwork, quality, and a positive working atmosphere are key. On top of that, you can enjoy a delicious hot lunch every working day.

As a Production Worker in the warehouse, you will help ensure that all goods are processed efficiently and accurately. Your tasks will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking and packing customer orders;
- Checking products for quality;
- Unpacking boxes and processing incoming goods;
- Sorting clothing and accessories;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

This is a full-time position in a 2-shift rotation:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM - 03:30 PM
- Afternoon shift: 03:00 PM - 11:30 PM

But there is also a nightshift you can work if you want from 23:00 tot 07:30. And there is work in the weekends!

- (Basic) English communication skills, or Polish or Spanish;
- Availability for full-time work in a 2-shift schedule;
- Ability to work effectively in a team;
- Physically fit and comfortable performing active warehouse work;
- Attention to detail and ability to follow instructions;
- Previous logistics or warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

- Packing and repacking products into cardboard export boxes;
- Preparing creams in a 400-liter mixing tank according to established formulas;
- Operating filling machines for tubes, wound care products, and FFP2 face masks;
- Replenishing raw materials and production supplies;
- Accurately completing production and quality documentation;
- Identifying and resolving minor technical issues;
- Setting up and changing over production lines;
- Supporting warehouse operations when needed;
- Working in accordance with CE, FDA, and cleanroom guidelines;
- Contributing ideas for process improvements and preventing recurring technical issues.

The company places a strong emphasis on independence. You will be trained to operate multiple machines and production stations independently as part of your development within the organization.

- Holds at least a VAPRO A diploma or an equivalent qualification;
- Speaks and writes either Dutch or English;
- Has technical insight and can analyze and solve equipment malfunctions;
- Works accurately, takes responsibility, and can work independently;
- Feels comfortable in an environment where quality standards and procedures are important;
- Brings discipline, energy, and a positive attitude to work.

Are you an experienced Reach Truck Driver looking for a new opportunity? We are currently recruiting for a modern logistics company in Helmond. As a Reach Truck Driver, you will be responsible for safely and efficiently moving goods throughout the warehouse while supporting daily logistics operations using modern equipment.

Your responsibilities:

- Operating a reach truck at heights of up to 12 meters;
- Moving and storing pallets throughout the warehouse;
- Picking orders using the reach truck;
- Scanning, labeling, and wrapping pallets;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Supporting Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule may be required. (6:00-15:00/15:00-00:00)

- Holds a valid Reach Truck certificate;
- Is comfortable working at heights up to 12 meters;
- Fulltime available;
- Living nearby Helmond, Mierlo, Geldrop, Nuenen or Eindhoven;
- Has experience in logistics and safety;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English.

As a Logistics Employee, you will start your journey in the Value Added Services (VAS) department. Together with your team, you will make sure products are processed accurately, packed properly and prepared for shipment to customers around the world.

- Inspect incoming goods;
- Load and unload containers;
- Label and repack products when needed;
- Pick, check and prepare customer orders for shipment;
- Work closely with your colleagues to ensure everything runs smoothly.

After approximately two months, you will move to another logistics department. Here, you will learn new tasks and gain even more variety in your work. This gives you the opportunity to develop yourself into an all-round logistics employeeDo you see yourself working in a dynamic logistics environment where you can develop your skills and grow within the company? Don’t wait any longer and apply today! We will contact you as soon as possible to discuss the opportunities.

Because you will also be working with an electric pallet truck (EPT) in this position, if you do not have any prior experience with it, you will be required to complete a training course and obtain the corresponding certificate.

- You speak and understand English well;
- You are available to work full-time;
- You are willing to work in a two-shift schedule after your training period;
- You have experience working in logistics or production;
- You are motivated and enjoy working hands-on.
- Holds an EPT certificate or is willing to obtain one through Olympia.

As an Industrial Cleaning Specialist, your primary responsibility is to clean and prepare returned packaging materials for reuse. This includes removing stickers, barcodes, and labels, as well as occasionally disassembling and reassembling products. The job is both physically active and varied, offering you new challenges every day. If you thrive on being hands-on and enjoy an active role, this is the perfect opportunity for you.

Your key tasks include:

- Cleaning formwork and other packaging materials;
- Removing stickers, barcodes, and labels without damaging surfaces;
- Disassembling and reassembling products as needed.

You’ll work in two shifts: early (06:00–15:00) and late (15:00–00:00), ensuring flexibility and variety in your schedule.

- Proficiency in English;
- Physical fitness and ability to perform active work throughout the day;
- Availability for two-shift work without exceptions.

Are you a hands-on worker, do you like working in an organized way, and do you feel at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to be part of one of Europe’s largest producers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position at our client in Waalwijk is perfect for you!

As a Logistics Employee, you play an important role in the logistics process surrounding the production of high-quality, custom-made sandwich panels for, among others, the bodywork industry and the defense sector. You ensure that materials, raw materials, and finished products are available at the right place and at the right time.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, in a close-knit team of colleagues. Order, overview, and safety are central to your daily tasks.

As a Logistics Employee, your tasks include:

- Loading and unloading goods using a forklift;

- Receiving and assisting drivers (first point of contact);

- Packing and preparing finished products for shipment;

- Managing internal logistics between the warehouse and production departments;

- Supplying raw materials to various production departments;

- Cleaning and organizing the warehouse and production halls;

- Ensuring a safe and tidy workplace.

Requirements

- You work in a structured manner and have an eye for order and safety;

- You hold a valid forklift certificate;

- You are a true team player;

- You have a good command of the Dutch or English language.
